- text:  Engine Compartment Inspection 9 items  Cylinder condition ▶ critical Check cylinders for leaks or cracks, especially around injector nozzles (fuel injected) and spark plug holes. Look for evidence of overheating.
- button "Pass"
- button "Flag"
- button "Fail"
- text: Crankcase inspection ▶ critical Check for cracks on top of the crankcase and at cylinder base bolts. Check rear case for leaks that may indicate a crankcase crack.
- button "Pass"
- button "Flag"
- button "Fail"
- text: Engine mounts ▶ critical Check rubber engine mounts for sagging, cracking, or deterioration. Check heat deflectors for wear and cutting into mount legs.
- button "Pass"
- button "Flag"
- button "Fail"
- text: Baffles Check condition of all baffles, especially hard, cracked, or missing pieces. Proper baffling is critical for cooling.
- button "Pass"
- button "Flag"
- button "Fail"
- text: Hoses, clamps and brackets ▶ critical Check all hoses for cracks, kinks, age, or bulging. Check clamps and brackets for broken, loose or missing items. Check fuel injector line grommets.
- button "Pass"
- button "Flag"
- button "Fail"
- text: Exhaust system ▶ critical Check for cracks, leaks, or dents. Check for missing mounting nuts or studs. Look for loose, bent, or collapsed clamps. Check for corrosion throughout.
- button "Pass"
- button "Flag"
- button "Fail"
- text: Muffler condition ▶ critical Check exterior for dents, heat warp, holes or cracks. Check for missing or distorted flame cones. Inspect tailpipe hangers at firewall.
- button "Pass"
